    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0814" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-04T19:00:00+01:00">November 4, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 5—3:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1913. From Murphy.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d712-f1"/> I am informed by a responsible
                    American correspondent that he learned from what he considers a reliable source
                    that Bogomolov<anchor n="9" xml:id="d712-f2"/> told de Gaulle<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d712-f3"/> a week before it was announced that France would not be a
                    member of the new European Advisory Commission to sit in London, but for de
                    Gaulle not to worry; Russia would see that France was taken care of. This
                    correspondent added that he was told de Gaulle’s reaction to the incident was
                    that Russia was seeking to play off the French against the Americans and
                    British, and in increasing suspicion of Russian support. This report is passed
                    along for what it may be worth, without definite evaluation.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department, repeated to London. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d712-f1" n="8" xml:id="d712-f1-content">
                <p>Robert D. Murphy, Personal Representative of President Roosevelt in North Africa;
                    Chief Civil Affairs Officer at Algiers; and U.S. Political Adviser, staff of the
                    Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d712-f2" n="9" xml:id="d712-f2-content">
                <p>Alexander Efremovich Bogomolov, Soviet Ambassador to the Allied Governments in
                    Exile at London.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d712-f3" n="10" xml:id="d712-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Charles de Gaulle, President of the French National Committee in London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
